<Base title="Methodology"><article class="article"><p class="eyebrow">METHODS / PILOT 001</p><h1>Make the boundaries visible.</h1><h2>One question, one frozen investigation</h2><p>Source reading and literature assessment were performed by the agent. Retrieval, quotation checks, protocol freezing, container execution, result export and static-site generation are implemented in code. This pilot does not yet provide autonomous broad literature discovery or continuous watching.</p><h2>Before execution</h2><p>The broker permits only configured HTTPS sources, with bounded retrieval sizes and timeouts. Rights and exact source quotation checks run outside the research container. The plan binds input hashes, code hash, a pinned runtime, resource budgets and the complete analysis family before the first model outcome is inspected.</p><h2>The comparison</h2><p>Two fixed ridge regressions predict the anomaly six months ahead from six monthly lags. One adds sine/cosine of the issue month and interactions with the latest anomaly. Persistence is a third, untrained reference. Models train on targets ending in 2014. Holdout issue dates start in 2015. No fitting, tuning or model selection uses holdout outcomes.</p><h2>Uncertainty</h2><p>Paired circular calendar-year block resampling uses 2-, 3- and 4-year blocks. The frozen rule requires a 5% RMSE benefit over both comparators and positive lower interval endpoints at every block length. The sample contains few ENSO cycles and the intervals cannot establish future skill.</p><h2>Five separate statuses</h2><dl>{Object.entries(pilot.question.statuses).map(([key,state])=><div><dt>{key}</dt><dd>{state.replaceAll('_',' ')}</dd></div>)}</dl><h2>Isolation and validation</h2><p>The research image has no network, host mounts or credentials. It runs as an unprivileged user with a read-only root filesystem. Identical results were generated in fresh containers. These checks demonstrate computational repeatability. They are not scientific peer review.</p><h2>Public disclosure gate</h2><p>This website is a local review preview. The publication bundle has a content hash. A public PR would already disclose its contents, so human approval must match the exact bundle before a public upload. Changes invalidate an earlier approval. No public push or deployment has occurred.</p><p><a href="/data/v1/plan.json">Inspect the frozen protocol ↗</a></p></article></Base>
